# The dGPU (RTX 3070 Mobile) never enters runtime sleep. It overrides 71-nvidia.rules, which
# sets "auto" when the driver binds.
# Why: the card's firmware fails to come back from runtime sleep ("failed to wait for GFW_BOOT",
# then Xid 119/154 and "GPU requires reset"). Seen on 2026-11-03, 11-10 (twice) and reproduced
# on 2026-11-11 within three forced wake-ups under CPU load. A card in that state hangs the next
# reboot on a black screen until someone holds the power button (2 of 2), and this machine is
# the only CI agent. Cost: the card idles awake instead of off; two clean rounds of cpu-ab.sh
# showed no loss of CPU work at the 40 W limit beyond the spread between rounds.
ACTION=="bind", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x10de", ATTR{class}=="0x030000", TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
ACTION=="bind", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x10de", ATTR{class}=="0x030200", TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="on"
